I agree with the poster.  NH3.0 is too hard.  Where's the fun in
getting killed suddenly and without any chance to do anything
about it?  If it only happened occasionally, I wouldn't complain.
However, I have been killed over and over by stupid things like
a killer bee or soldier ant, or having a ratwere appear, summon help,
and dispatch me summarily to nethack heaven.  I agree that version
2.3 was too easy, and I really like the new features of 3.0, but
somehow it has to be made easier, especially at the beginning.

It seems to me that having a good armor class does not do as much
good as it should.  Apparently, no matter *what* the armor
class is there is always a substantial chance of a hit.  For example,
walking into a room full of Uruk-Hai's is virtually impossible to 
survive without substantial magic (wands, etc.)  If they ever get their
hands on you, kiss it good-bye.  (Should Elbereth protect against
poisoned arrows?)

I have almost sworn off nethack several times after being pissed off by
once again getting killed arbitrarily on a good game.  I keep coming 
back because it *is* a good game!

Any ideas on ways to decrease the frustration level?

